        "original_id": "4cc88fab-605d-59da-8ff6-bc67380480ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Viney\n- Groups: The Band\n- Songs: \"Chest Fever\", \"The Weight\"\n- Albums: Music from Big Pink\n- Companies: Capitol Records\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, The Band released \"The Weight\" as Capitol Records single 2269.\n- In 1968, The Band included \"The Weight\" on its debut album Music from Big Pink.\n- Peter Viney identified \"Chest Fever\" as the Music from Big Pink track that appeared on most later live albums and compilations.\n- Peter Viney stated that only \"The Weight\" surpassed \"Chest Fever\" in later live album and compilation appearances.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5b2985e1-f5c2-576e-b7a2-c314c83f04b7",
        "text": "Page: Chest Fever. Sentence: It is, according to Peter Viney, a historian of the group, \"the Big Pink track that has appeared on most subsequent live albums and compilations\", second only to \"The Weight\".\nPage: The Weight. Sentence: \"The Weight\" is a song originally by the Canadian-American group The Band that was released as Capitol Records single 2269 in 1968 and on the group's debut album \"Music from Big Pink\".",
